        1395
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "super-clan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_western_desert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan recognizes Dong clan’s Red River Wheel. The Immortal Gu House came from a mysterious inheritance, and in his previous life it displayed great power and gained huge fame. Dong clan Gu Immortals take molten flame birds that would strengthen Red River Wheel’s speed.",
      "chapters": [
        1708
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "house-origin-and-upgrade",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Di Chang thinks of earth path methods and notes that Dong clan specializes in earth path when considering whether an attack is Dong clan’s revenge.",
      "chapters": [
        1780
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "earth-path-specialty",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_di_chang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Central Continent conflict pulls Western Desert forces in, Dong clan still mobilizes rank seven Immortal Gu House Red River Wheel. Dong clan is a Western Desert righteous path force and hates Western Desert’s demons the most, so its Gu Immortals inside Red River Wheel gnash their teeth at Wan Zi Hong.",
      "chapters": [
        1925
